{"name":"Gibraltar","hex":"#626970","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gibraltar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A peninsula, city, and overseas territory of the United Kingdom, at the southern end of Iberia.","A strait connecting the Mediterranean to the Atlantic between Gibraltar and Morocco; in full, Strait of Gibraltar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":[";  A cortado served in a small glass;  any cortado"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gibraltar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gibraltar","blocks":[{"text":"Gibraltar is a British Overseas Territory and city located at the southern tip of the Iberian Peninsula, on the Bay of Gibraltar, near the exit of the Mediterranean Sea into the Atlantic Ocean. It has an area of 6.8 km2 (2.6 sq mi) and is bordered to the north by Spain. The landscape is dominated by the Rock of Gibraltar, at the foot of which is a densely populated town area. Gibraltar is home to around 38,000 people, primarily Gibraltarians."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Flag_of_Gibraltar.svg/330px-Flag_of_Gibraltar.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibraltar","wikidata":"Q1410"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Gibraltar5.jpg/500px-Gibraltar5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Gibraltar5.jpg/1280px-Gibraltar5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Gibraltar5.jpg/500px-Gibraltar5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An aerial view","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGibraltar5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Gibraltar_aerial_view_looking_northwest.jpg